PART 2  THE COSMIC TOTAL -- the committed budget x the line, per unit rate
==========================================================================================================
  committed budget: rho_dm,0 = Omega_dm rho_crit,0 = 2.250e-27 kg/m^3 (Planck; free dust ~98% of the dark sector, G079)
  the LOCAL (z=0) shell -- the line at observed E = 2.544 keV:
    dI/dE|_E / Gamma = (1/4 pi)(rho_dm,0/m)(c/H0)/E = 1.065e+26 ph cm^-2 s^-1 sr^-1 keV^-1 per (Gamma = 1 s^-1)
    in a resolution element dE = 5 eV (XRISM-class): 5.327e+23 ph cm^-2 s^-1 sr^-1 per (Gamma = 1 s^-1)
    in dE = 60 eV (CCD/eROSITA-class): 6.393e+24 ph cm^-2 s^-1 sr^-1 per (Gamma = 1 s^-1)
  the FULL cosmic integral (all shells, photons land at E/(1+z) BELOW the line -- a sub-2.54-keV continuum, not the line):
    I_tot / Gamma = 9.687e+25 ph cm^-2 s^-1 sr^-1 per (Gamma = 1 s^-1)

  vs THE X-RAY BACKGROUND (ALL UNVERIFIED literature -- the 3.5-keV line class):
    Gruber+99 CXB I(E) = 7.877 E^-1.29 ph cm^-2 s^-1 sr^-1 keV^-1 (UNVERIFIED):
      at 2.54 keV: 2.361  |  at 3.5 keV: 1.565
    the 3.5-keV line class (UNVERIFIED): Bulbul+14 claimed ~5e-5 ph cm^-2 s^-1 sr^-1 in stacked clusters;
      Hitomi ruled the Perseus line out at >99% CL (Aharonian+17); Dessert-Rodd-Safdi+20 stacked galaxies bound sin^2 2theta <~ 1e-11;
      eROSITA 'new strong constraints below 5 keV' (A05).  The class limit: I_line <~ 1e-5 ph cm^-2 s^-1 sr^-1.
    framework line per unit rate vs these: dI/dE = 1.07e+26 ph cm^-2 s^-1 sr^-1 keV^-1 per s^-1
      -> the line EQUALS the CXB continuum (2.4 ph cm^-2 s^-1 sr^-1 keV^-1) when Gamma ~ 2.22e-26 s^-1
      (tau ~ 1.0e+08 t_H); equals the 3.5-class limit 1e-5 when Gamma ~ 1.88e-29 s^-1

